{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "0d3f5c1a-9a6e-4a71-8c2f-1b7e5a0c4d21",
    "name": "Lipid Class Classifier API",
    "description": "API-level tests for the Lipid Class Classifier backend.\n\nRun against a live stack:\n\n    docker compose up -d --wait\n\nThe requests run in order and chain state through collection variables: registration stores `token` and `email`, upload stores `jobId`. Import the environment file `lipid-classifier.local.postman_environment.json` alongside this collection.\n\nOne manual step: the upload requests use a file body. Postman does not carry file contents inside an exported collection, so open each upload request, go to Body > form-data, and re-select the `file` value:\n\n  - 'Upload mzML spectrum'  ->  testdata/sample.mzML\n  - 'Upload rejected extension'  ->  testdata/wrong-extension.txt\n\nBoth files are produced by `python3 testdata/generate_fixtures.py`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh address per run keeps the collection re-runnable against a persistent database.",
                  "const email = `postman-${Date.now()}@example.com`;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('email', email);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('password', 'password123');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds 201 Created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('returns a token and the created user', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token').that.is.a('string').and.is.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('the email is normalised to lower case', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('email').toLowerCase());",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('the token is a three part JWT', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token.split('.')).to.have.lengthOf(3);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates an account and returns a bearer token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('returns a token for the same account', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.user.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userId'));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Continue the run with the login token rather than the registration one.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login with surrounding whitespace and mixed case",
          "event": [
